TCP Port Scanner — Educational Purpose / Professional Usage

TCP connect-based port checks for Termux and Linux. Root not required.
Use only against systems you own or are explicitly authorized to test.

Usage:
  bash src/functions/tcp401.sh 127.0.0.1 --authorized
  bash src/functions/tcp401.sh 192.168.1.10 --authorized --ports 22,80,443
  bash src/functions/tcp401.sh example.org --authorized --allow-public --ports 80,443 --json

Default: 19 common ports; max 128 ports, 8 workers, 3-second timeout.
Only 256 address/port combinations per invocation.
No stealth, exploitation, firewall evasion or rate-limit bypass.
Results: OPEN or CLOSED_OR_FILTERED; not vulnerability findings.
Privacy: scan only within your legal authorization, avoid collecting
personal data without a lawful basis, and minimize stored results.
